    "Gemini 4 Neon ($3 / $15, index 61) scores above the listed flagship Gemini 4 Carbon; once Carbon and Argon double to $4 / $20 on 1 Dec, Neon is both cheaper and higher-scored.",
    "Only models with an Artificial Analysis score are listed. Left out for lack of one: Kimi K3 and K2.7 Code (Moonshot), Grok 4.3 and grok-build (xAI), GLM-5.3-FlashX (Z.ai), Ministral 3 (Mistral), and older generations of every provider. Tencent, Moonshot and xAI therefore show one model each.",
    "Mistral Medium 3.5 (index 5) and Meta Muse Glimmer (index 6) are scored but have no list price on their vendors' pages, so they are left out. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next is listed without a price for the same reason.",
    "Speed for the flagship rows comes from OpenRouter live traffic; for the added rows it comes from modelgrep, which republishes OpenRouter data. The two differ by a few tokens per second on the same model.",
    "Meta prices come from OpenRouter listings (Meta's own page showed none); Anthropic and Moonshot prices come from third-party trackers.",
    "Gemini 3.8 Flash doubles to $1.50 / $7.50 on 1 Jan 2027. Google's batch tier is half the listed price.",
